TurboSerial examples
====================

These examples use the public TurboSerial ABI from `turbo_serial.h`.
They do not include `libserialport.h` or call `sp_*` APIs directly.
The examples are regular executables; they are not registered as CTest cases
because most of them require real serial hardware or a configured virtual port.

Examples
--------

- `list_ports.c` - creates a port-list snapshot and prints visible port names.
- `port_info.c` - reads metadata for one named port.
- `port_config.c` - configures and opens one serial handle.
- `send_receive.c` - performs blocking write/read on one open handle.
- `await_events.c` - waits for readiness through a TurboSerial event set.
- `handle_errors.c` - handles `turbo_serial_result_t` at the application boundary.

Build
-----

Configure the repository first, then build the aggregate examples target:

```text
cmake --preset win-release-user
cmake --build --preset win-release-user --target turbo_serial_examples
```

The generated executables are written to `build/Msvc-Release/bin`:

```text
build/Msvc-Release/bin/example_list_ports.exe
build/Msvc-Release/bin/example_port_info.exe COM1
```

Run
---

Most examples need a port name. For example:

```text
build/Msvc-Release/bin/example_port_config.exe COM3
build/Msvc-Release/bin/example_send_receive.exe COM3
build/Msvc-Release/bin/example_await_events.exe COM3
```

Validation
----------

The examples are compile-checked through the `turbo_serial_examples` target.
TurboSerial tests include the public ABI test, libserialport regression tests,
and a mocked backend test that drives the async SPSC pump without hardware:

```text
cmake -S . -B build\Msvc-Release -DENABLE_TESTS=ON -DBUILD_TESTS=ON -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=ON
cmake --build --preset win-release-user --target turbo_serial test_serialport test_turbo_serial_public_abi test_turbo_serial_mock
ctest --preset win-release-user -R "test_serialport|test_turbo_serial_public_abi|test_turbo_serial_mock" --output-on-failure
```
